  "summary": "Conservative Boris Johnson unseated the two-term incumbent Ken Livingstone (Labour) to become the second Mayor of London. Johnson won 1,044,068 first-preference votes (43.2%) to Livingstone's 894,316 (37.0%), and was elected with 1,168,738 votes (53.2%) to 1,028,966 (46.8%) after second preferences. Turnout jumped almost nine points to 44.6%. The Conservatives became the largest Assembly party with 11 seats, and the BNP won its first \u2014 and only \u2014 London-wide seat.",
